From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:47:47 -0400
Subject: put Clear on the line between pinned and unpinned tabs

The first DMG put the Clear row above the new-tab button at the bottom of the
sidebar. The reference puts it on the hairline that separates pinned tabs from
the rest, near the top, and the operator called the bottom placement out.

The hairline is TabStripView's existing separator, which its layout positions
by pointer and type -- so the affordance is a views::Separator subclass swapped
in at construction, painting a hairline with Clear at the trailing end when the
region view wires a callback, and the stock separator otherwise. Upstream only
showed that separator when the strip was collapsed; it now shows whenever
pinned and unpinned tabs both exist, since it carries the affordance.

Clear closes the unpinned tabs of the active Space, collected before any close
because closing shifts every index behind it.

Why: operator feedback; the reference's Clear separates pinned from unpinned.
Removable when: the sidebar's sections are restructured wholesale (per-Space
pins, New Tab above the list), at which point this moves with them.
